        },
        "body": "graphql-js merges overlapping fields when they have the same arguments, but not if the values come from different variables, even if the variables have the same value.\n\nFor example, given variables: `{ \"orderBy\": \"NAME_ASC\", \"orderBy2\": \"NAME_ASC\" }` this merges without problems:\n\n```\nquery ($orderBy: _GroupOrdering) {\n  viewer {\n    allGroups(orderBy: $orderBy) { count }\n    allGroups(orderBy: $orderBy) { count }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBut this fails with `Fields \"allGroups\" conflict because they have differing arguments.`:\n\n```\nquery ($orderBy: _GroupOrdering, $orderBy2: _GroupOrdering) {\n  viewer {\n    allGroups(orderBy: $orderBy) { count }\n    allGroups(orderBy: $orderBy2) { count }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis is an issue when using Relay because it can produce queries like this in some cases.\n\nThe relevant line of code seems to be here: https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/blob/a6bcc75d3c19ce31847cd77279a41fbc6ac032d2/src/validation/rules/OverlappingFieldsCanBeMerged.js#L209 It only compares the names of variables. Should we also take the variable values in account when validating if the fields can be merged?\n",
